From: Armada <no-reply@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: A722 has no LPAC

The A722 has no low-priority async compute pipe, so leave has_lpac off
for it. Qualcomm's KGSL lists no ADRENO_LPAC feature for the A722
(gen7_17_0) and puts it in the gen7_14_0 family, which has neither BV
nor LPAC:
https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/kgsl/blob/2b2d762c0b843c560d2ae2203f6b3cfe1474fb3f/adreno-gpulist.h#L2920
https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/kgsl/blob/2b2d762c0b843c560d2ae2203f6b3cfe1474fb3f/adreno.h#L1520
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
index e805e9f..fa893cc 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1119,7 +1119,8 @@ add_gpus([
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff43020100, name="Adreno (TM) 722"),
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A7XX,
-        [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen1, GPUProps(no_bv = True)],
+        [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen1, GPUProps(no_bv = True,
+                                        has_lpac = False)],
         num_ccu = 2,
         tile_align_w = 64,
         tile_align_h = 16,
